Nearby, I see a fruit stall.
A woman is selling fresh mangoes there.
The mangoes look very beautiful.
She looks at me and smiles.
She cuts a small piece of a yellow mango.
Then she gives it to me.
"Try eating this," she says.
I taste the mango.
It is very sweet!
"This is very tasty," I say.
"One kilo is eighty rupees," the woman says.
I open my cloth bag.
"I need one kilo of mangoes," I say.
"Please pack one kilo."
She packs the mangoes nicely.
I take a hundred-rupee note from my purse.
I give the money to her.
She gives me twenty rupees back as change.
I thank her.
I happily take the mangoes.
